# name: push_ball_to_goal
# description: push the ball to the goal point you marked
# triggers: push the ball to the goal, push the ball there, push the ball to the mark, push ball to goal, ball to the goal, push it to the goal, push the ball to the spot, push the ball to that point
# plan: locate the ball (scan)@SCAN_FOR | line up behind the ball & push it to your goal@PUSH_TO_GOAL
#
# The goal is the point a HUMAN marked: tick the Ball-goal box in the web UI and
# click the BEV (or POST /set_ball_goal). Each round the robot finds the ball,
# marks it, drives to the point BEHIND it on the goal-ball line (or briefly
# backs up if already behind it and the rear lidar path is clear), squares up,
# and shoves FORWARD - then re-measures and repeats. A crooked shove is corrected
# by the next round instead of compounding. Hard-code a goal in odom metres with
# PUSH_TO_GOAL(x, y) instead.

SET ball = SCAN_FOR("ball", 360)
IF ball != NONE THEN
    PRINT "Found the ball - pushing it to the goal you marked."
    SET r = PUSH_TO_GOAL()
    PRINT "Result:"
    PRINT r
ELSE
    PRINT "No ball found in the room."
END
